- op: discuss  # b806
  at: '2026-05-12T07:37:59Z'  # b806
  by: agent  # b806
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b806
  clock: 3  # b806
  nonce: b806  # b806
  message: "Fixed in PR (commit 86dd5c3fe0). Same BUG-04/05 shape as WI-milak / WI-kunoz applied to route_handler's symbol_by_name primary index. The pre-existing partial mitigation prefers non-route over route on dict overwrite, but non-route vs non-route collisions stayed silent: two Django views named list_users, two Express functions named list, two un-qualified Ruby methods named index — all silently shadow each other under the single-value dict.\n\nFix (conservative INV-zuhub-conformant minimum): link_routes_to_handlers builds name_collisions: frozenset[str] up front (names and meta.qualified_name keys shared by 2+ non-route symbols). At each successful handler resolution (main dispatches_to AND React Router loader/action), the resolved Symbol's name + qualified_name are checked against name_collisions; a hit drops the edge to confidence=0.5 + meta.disambiguation_fallback=True. The six internal resolvers (_resolve_rails/laravel/phoenix/express/django/go_handler) keep their existing signatures — the conformance is enforced at the caller, not by changing resolution logic. Edge.create calls use the canonical IfExp + dict-spread pattern so the L4 walker statically gates the conformance.\n\n5 new property tests under TestINVZuhubConformanceForRouteHandler. All existing route-handler tests stay green. Smart-test: 3104 passed. check-package-coverage: 100% across all 5 packages. L4 fallback-coherence walker: clean.\n\nThe audit's optional precision improvement (extend multi-value symbols_by_short_name to all resolution paths, or scope primary index by (file_path, symbol_name)) remains future work; the conformance gate is closed. Empirical re-confirmation candidate on multi-namespace Rails monorepos (chatwoot, mastodon-style) for the next BVT cycle.\n\nCompletes the four-item BUG-04/05 audit batch (siblings WI-jifiv PR #3650, WI-patiz PR #3651, WI-fujum closed as already-done by WI-harim)."  # b806
